## Goal
Get Portero to a first locally runnable and testable version: a macOS link handler app that receives URLs (kAEGetURL) with the opener's bundle id, plus default-browser registration, iCloud sync, rules initialization, and app bundle build and install.

## Problems
- Links clicked inside a browser can't be intercepted; the handler only sees links from other apps. Documented in the README and tracked in a Linear issue for a future browser extension.
- The first app test logged the opener as unknown ("-"), unlike the CLI run, which recorded the Terminal bundle id.
- The bundle was built from a dirty tree, so the version reads "-dirty".
- Test tabs opened in Dia had to be closed manually via AppleScript.

## Decision
- Handler in cgo/ObjC (`internal/handler`) with a non-darwin stub, which keeps the Go core portable.
- `cmd/portero/app.go` shares one routing path between the CLI and the app: load rules, route, launch, write to decisions.log.
- `scripts/build-app.sh` builds the bundle with an Info.plist (http/https, LSUIElement). It is installed to ~/Applications, with the CLI in ~/.local/bin.
- Added default-browser, sync (iCloud Drive) and rules init commands. Verified live: the app opened a test URL in Dia/Private, and init wrote a 4-rule config.

## Rejected
